Lab follow-up for #867830, not part of the issue's patch (drupal-core-lab, 2026-11-06).

The #306 re-roll (867830-unpublished-style-of, 0fcbb553) removes the MARK_READ, MARK_NEW and MARK_UPDATED constants from
core/includes/theme.inc but leaves the 'mark' theme hook definition in ThemeCommonElements.php defaulting 'status' to MARK_NEW.
On core 422099995ecf every page then fails with: Error: Undefined constant "Drupal\Core\Theme\MARK_NEW" in
core/lib/Drupal/Core/Theme/ThemeCommonElements.php line 136 (the theme registry is rebuilt on the first request after a cache clear).
This patch only lets the rest of the change be evaluated: 'status' defaults to NULL and the 'type' variable the patched templates
print is declared. It is applied after the issue's patch on the After side only, and is named in BRANCHES.md and EVIDENCE.md.

diff --git a/core/lib/Drupal/Core/Theme/ThemeCommonElements.php b/core/lib/Drupal/Core/Theme/ThemeCommonElements.php
index 50755c3..c41f829 100644
--- a/core/lib/Drupal/Core/Theme/ThemeCommonElements.php
+++ b/core/lib/Drupal/Core/Theme/ThemeCommonElements.php
@@ -133,7 +133,8 @@ class ThemeCommonElements {
       ],
       'mark' => [
         'variables' => [
-          'status' => MARK_NEW,
+          'status' => NULL,
+          'type' => NULL,
         ],
       ],
       'item_list' => [
